This commit implements a complete machine learning workflow for classifying mushrooms using a Random Forest classifier. The notebook begins with loading the Mushroom dataset from the UCI Machine Learning Repository and assigning explicit column names due to the absence of headers in the raw data.

All categorical features are converted into numerical form using Label Encoding to make the data suitable for machine learning algorithms. The dataset is then separated into features and target variables and split into training and testing sets to ensure reliable model evaluation.

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) is performed to understand the dataset’s structure and feature relationships. This includes examining dataset information, visualizing class distribution using count plots, and analyzing feature correlations through a heatmap.

Finally, a Random Forest classifier is trained on the training data and evaluated on the test data using accuracy score. The results demonstrate that the model performs effectively on the dataset, confirming the suitability of Random Forest for this classification task.
